diff --git a/architecture/security-policy.md b/architecture/security-policy.md
index 36a9195..004702e 100644
--- a/architecture/security-policy.md
+++ b/architecture/security-policy.md
@@ -509,3 +509,43 @@ to match, so reuse cannot transfer ownership between process generations.
 Retired PID evidence is discarded; established identity, activity, and
 correlation-vector links remain eligible during the five-second late-event
 window. Records without matching generation evidence fail closed.
+
+## Ordin request integrity extension
+
+This local extension to source revision `6648bd0c290efbc41ba131ee9831ee45cd431f94`
+adds `request_integrity: {algorithm, commitments}` to an inspected endpoint.
+The algorithm is `ordin.authority-json.sha256.v1`. Each lowercase SHA-256 value
+commits a bounded JSON authority tree, without storing argument values.
+GraphQL commits the complete request envelope or ordered batch; JSON-RPC and
+MCP commit method, parameters, request/notification kind, and batch order while
+omitting correlation ID values. Duplicate decoded keys are rejected. Decimal
+values preserve exact numeric precision, integer/decimal distinctions and signed
+decimal zero; object key order is neutral and Unicode normalization is preserved.
+
+The endpoint requires `enforcement: enforce` and inspected TLS. A committed
+request must use POST, contain no URL query delimiter, and request no upgrade.
+The complete buffered body must match an allowed commitment before policy
+admission and again after middleware and credential transformations. Mismatches
+deny regardless of audit behavior and produce value-free denial diagnostics.
+The matched commitment is emitted in structured OCSF only after upstream write.
+Coarse operation/method rules and the commitment must both allow the request.
+
+Limits are 1 MiB raw/framed bytes, 4096 nodes, depth 32, 128 items per JSON
+container, 65536 UTF-8 bytes per string, 1024 significant integer/decimal digits,
+and decimal exponents of magnitude at most 10000. The domain prefix does not
+count toward the framed-byte budget. Parser-specific protocol limits remain
+explicit endpoint configuration. Overlapping endpoints must agree on integrity
+configuration; malformed or ambiguous reloads cannot activate a partial gate.
+
+Exact TCP IP literals additionally require a destination IP/CIDR allowlist and
+the authenticated, confirmed native staged mediation properties
+`seccomp-notify` and `seccomp-notify-procfs`. The supervisor reports those
+properties only after boundary confirmation, using the captured configuration
+revision and instance fence. The legacy DNS-only transparent path does not grant
+literal traffic. Protected metadata, loopback, link-local and unspecified
+destinations remain blocked.
+
+Runtime management reports the CLI, gateway and supervisor source identities.
+An operator must require the audited extension identity and exact build
+manifest; an OpenShell version string alone does not establish this feature.
+Rebuild and embed both the guest sandbox and host supervisor in the VM driver.
